    <entry xml:lang="en">
        <title>The Little Things</title>
        <published>2021-11-28T00:00:00+00:00</published>
        <updated>2021-11-28T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
        
        <author>
          <name>Michael Park</name>
        </author>
        
        <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://mhpark.me/posts/the-little-things/"/>
        <id>https://mhpark.me/posts/the-little-things/</id>
        
        <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;The dozens of predictions that economists have been making over the last two
years centers around this idea that once everything returns to a certain level
of &lt;em&gt;normal&lt;/em&gt; - probably better to use safe instead of normal but I&#39;m sure we all
agree &lt;em&gt;normal&lt;/em&gt; means something different than it used to - consumers are going
to start splurging on all the money they have been saving up. Personally, even
if this turns out to be the case eventually, I think this saga of our
lives really has given us enjoyment in the little things.&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
        
    </entry>
